\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 10.5 Effort and Coaching Signals\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 Cramapple is a teaching system, not a homework grader. We do not need to police originality the way teacher-facing tools (EssayGrader, GraderAI, GPTZero, CoGrader) do \'97 there is no grade to defend and no academic-honesty case to make. What we do need is a layer of behavioral signal that improves the diagnostic, surfaces coaching moments in real time, and gives parents legitimate visibility into whether the incentives they are paying for are buying actual effort.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \

\f2\fs22 \cf3 Where the teacher-tool category is built on a defensive integrity posture (catch the cheaters, prove the originality), Cramapple takes a coaching posture (effort is a learning signal; "cheating" is a moment to coach about exam reality; parents have a stake). This is a deliberate differentiation from the incumbent feature set.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Three signals\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs22 \cf3 Time-on-task (primary). 
\f2\b0 How long the student spends on each Attempt, captured automatically. Quick correct responses signal mastery; slow correct responses signal earned understanding. Quick incorrect responses signal guessing or paste; slow incorrect responses signal genuine struggle. The Repair mode selection logic uses time-on-task as a diagnostic input alongside the error classification. A slow incorrect response defaults toward Show (the student tried hard but lacks the method); a fast incorrect response defaults toward Tighten with a coaching nudge about the rubric.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \

\f0\b\fs22 \cf3 Typing pattern (secondary). 
\f2\b0 Keystroke metadata during Attempt \'97 pauses, backspaces, deletion patterns, paste events, sustained rhythm. Authentic student writing produces a distinct signature that differs sharply from paste-and-edit behavior. Implementation is cheap (timestamp keystrokes, aggregate to a few summary features). Borrowed from GPTZero's writing-replay feature; repurposed here as coaching signal rather than detection.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \

\f0\b\fs22 \cf3 Text-pattern AI detection (tertiary). 
\f2\b0 Standard perplexity and burstiness checks on submitted text. Lower reliability than typing-pattern, since modern LLM output is increasingly close to human text in these dimensions, but useful as a secondary check when the typing signal is ambiguous.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Three uses\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs22 \cf3 In-product coaching prompts. 
\f2\b0 When the signals fire strongly \'97 paste event, near-zero typing time, suspiciously polished text \'97 Cramapple surfaces a prompt at the moment of submission. The functional intent is peer-voice, non-preachy: a friend catching a slip, not a system surveilling behavior. The prompt acknowledges the reality (you cannot take this shortcut on the actual exam) and treats the student as a peer making a choice. Specific tone and language belong to the brand-and-marketing workstream; this document specifies the functional intent only.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 The student can dismiss the prompt and proceed. The signal is calibrated to fire rarely and only on strong patterns. Repeated triggers downweight the response in the diagnostic but do not block participation.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs22 \cf3 Diagnostic input. 
\f2\b0 Responses that show strong paste signals are downweighted in the next-best-action engine. If Cramapple thinks the response is not the student's actual reasoning, it should not treat the resulting performance as a measurement of the student's actual proficiency. The student still gets their grade and feedback; the system just does not update its model of the student based on a response it has reason to think did not come from them.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \

\f0\b\fs22 \cf3 Parent visibility (opt-in). 
\f2\b0 For families using the vision's parent-incentive mechanism (where a parent offers a reward tied to practice goals or score targets), the effort signals roll up into a parent-facing summary. Time-on-task patterns, paste frequency, session completion. Framed positively as "your kid's effort patterns" rather than punitively, but honest. A parent paying for the tool and offering an additional incentive has a legitimate interest in knowing whether the kid is actually doing the work. The student can see exactly what the parent sees, and can opt the feature off; this preserves student agency while giving parents real information.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\fs18 \cf4 Decision: time-on-task and typing-pattern signals are built into Attempt at launch. Coaching prompts fire on strong signal combinations only. Parent-visibility rollup ships in the version that includes the incentive mechanism (timing per vision Section 9).
\f1\i0\fs24 \cf0 \

\f3\i\fs18 \cf4 Open: thresholds for "strong signal" calibration on real student data; specific design of the parent-facing rollup; whether to license a third-party AI-detection API or build an in-house perplexity check.
\f1\i0\fs24 \cf0 \
