\cf0 13. Data and Improvement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 Cramapple is a learning system that gets better when students use it. This section names the operating posture on student response data \'97 what we use, what we do not, and how we frame it to families.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 13.1 Posture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 The teacher-tool category of AI graders has converged on a defensive privacy posture: "we do not train AI models on student data." Fiveable, EssayGrader.ai, GraderAI, and CoGrader all publish a version of this commitment. The commitment exists because their customers are school districts, whose procurement teams require it for FERPA and COPPA compliance. The constraint is a competitive must-have in B2B EdTech.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \

\f2\fs22 \cf3 Cramapple is B2C. Our customers are families. Families have a different relationship with the question of how their student's responses are used. Most families want their kid's prep tool to keep getting smarter, and most accept that a smarter tool was built by learning from earlier students. The defensive "no training" framing is operationally limiting and competitively unnecessary.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \

\f2\fs22 \cf3 Cramapple's posture is the positive version: anonymized student responses help Cramapple improve grading accuracy and teach the next student more effectively. Student-supplied questions may additionally become public anonymous landing pages as described in Section 8. The model is honest, operationally enabling, and a competitive differentiator that no incumbent teacher tool can match.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 13.2 The Disclosure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 A single line of plain language at the point of contribution: "We use this anonymously to help other students." No opt-in or opt-out machinery, no elaborate consent flow. The disclosure is honest about what happens; the student or family that does not want it does not use Cramapple. The simplicity is itself the design \'97 overly-elaborate consent flows signal a defensive posture and degrade the customer relationship.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 13.3 What We Use, What We Do Not\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa60\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls23\ilvl0
\f4\i\b\fs22 \cf3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 We use, with anonymization: student responses to questions (FRQ text, MCQ choices, the optional "why" field), the grader's evaluation of those responses, aggregate behavioral signals (time-on-task, attempt patterns), and student-supplied questions when they pass the quality gate for landing-page publication.
\f1\i0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \ulnone \strike0\striked0 \
\ls23\ilvl0
\f4\i\b\fs22 \cf3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 We do not use: student names, account information, payment data, parent identifiers, or any combination of fields that would allow re-identification. Anonymization is implemented to a k-anonymity standard at minimum.
\f1\i0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \ulnone \strike0\striked0 \
\ls23\ilvl0
\f4\i\b\fs22 \cf3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 We do not share or sell: any data, anonymized or not, to third parties. The data is used solely to improve Cramapple itself.
\f1\i0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \ulnone \strike0\striked0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 13.4 Compliance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 Cramapple complies with COPPA (for users under 13), state student privacy laws, and the relevant GDPR provisions for international users. The compliance work is a tax of operating in the category, not a marketing claim. The framing in front of families is the positive value prop above; the legal posture sits in the privacy policy and is referenced when asked.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 13.5 Operating Implication\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 This posture has a concrete operating consequence: Cramapple builds a feedback loop where the grader's validation set grows over time. Orly's initial calibration uses released FRQs with known scores; ongoing improvement uses anonymized real student responses scored by Cramapple, periodically reviewed by Orly for drift detection. This is the mechanism by which the weighted Kappa launch gate of .60 can move toward the .70 aspiration over time.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\fs18 \cf4 Decision: anonymized student-response contribution is on by default with plain-language disclosure at signup. Student-supplied questions become public landing pages per Section 8 quality gating, with the same anonymous disclosure.
\f1\i0\fs24 \cf0 \
